Dear team,
3 of our developers were nominated for their achievement in Q2!

Rachel Freedman is nominated for her leadership and outstanding contribution to the CCM 4.2 upgrade initiative. She played a pivotal role in driving the project forward, leveraging her deep product and technical expertise to ensure a successful modernization effort while maintaining delivery quality and stability.
Beyond her direct technical contributions, Rachel actively embraced new practices around deployment process and artifacts management, helping raise the quality bar across the team. She has demonstrated a strong commitment to developing others by sharing her knowledge, mentoring teammates, and now supporting additional teams adopting similar approaches.

Roman Alekseev is nominated for his exceptional contribution to the Agentic Fabric development initiative, including the successful integration of the COE Agent as part of Orchestration version 11.3.0. He consistently demonstrates deep technical expertise, outstanding execution, and a strong commitment to delivering results that advance our platform innovation agenda.
Roman combines broad system knowledge with remarkable flexibility and ownership, readily stepping into the most critical areas of the project and delivering high-quality solutions under demanding timelines. He continuously pushes boundaries by embracing new technologies and implementation approaches, helping accelerate our Agentic AI roadmap.

Michael Margolis is nominated for his significant contribution to the React migration and modernization initiative. Starting as the sole developer driving the effort, Michael became a central figure in the growing team, providing technical leadership, guidance, and continuity throughout the project.
He played a key role in code reviews, refactoring activities, architectural alignment, and modernization efforts, helping establish best practices and improve overall code quality. Michael consistently demonstrates a team-first mindset, serving as a trusted support and synchronization point for the entire team while actively contributing to the development and success of others.

I am incredibly proud to work alongside such a talented and dedicated team. The achievements recognized today demonstrate what is possible when expertise, innovation, and teamwork come together. Congratulations to Rachel Freedman, Roman Alekseev, and Michael Margolis on this well-deserved recognition, and thank you to everyone for the passion and commitment you bring to our journey every day. Together, we continue to push boundaries and make a meaningful impact.




Alina Moshkovich

AVP Engineering, Orchestration.AI

